#   the honest criterion: these are third-party tags we cannot rebuild, so a
#   fixed version existing upstream in Go or a Go module does NOT help us until
#   the image publisher ships a new tag.
#
# ENTRY FORMAT
#   One `CVE-… exp:YYYY-MM-DD` line per waiver, preceded by its justification
#   comment block. Trivy suppresses the finding while `today < exp`, so an entry
#   whose exp: is today is ALREADY expired (Phase 812 fix). Renewal runs
#   daily so the window never lapses inside its own cron morning.
# =============================================================================

# kin-openapi nil-pointer dereference in openapi3filter.ValidateResponse: an
# OpenAPI document declaring a response header with `content` instead of
# `schema` passes validation, but every response validation for that operation
# then dereferences the nil schema and panics. No grafana tag fixes it (13.1.6
# and 13.2.4 both ship kin-openapi v0.144.0; fix is 0.146.0). Grafana runs on
# the internal monitoring network and never validates untrusted OpenAPI
# specifications, so the vulnerable path is unreachable.
#
# Carriers:
#   - grafana/grafana:13.2.4-ubuntu
# Reachability: internal-monitoring-only
# Severity: HIGH
# Re-check when: grafana ships kin-openapi >= 0.149.0
